# Cake staging: bite levels 0..6 live in rotation (setblock's 6th arg) —
# each bite trims 2px off the +x edge and the cut face draws the interior
# tile. Flat floor is SANDSTONE at y=0; AIR starts at y=1.
wait_idle 20 6000
setblock 4 1 8 CAKE 0
setblock 6 1 8 CAKE 2
setblock 8 1 8 CAKE 4
setblock 10 1 8 CAKE 6
# A plain candle sits in the row as the non-edible control.
setblock 12 1 8 BLACK_CANDLE 0
wait 30
assert_block 4 1 8 CAKE
assert_block 6 1 8 CAKE
assert_block 8 1 8 CAKE
assert_block 10 1 8 CAKE
# A neighbor write must not pop a bitten cake: rotation is the bite count,
# not a yaw, so the floor-support face must not rotate with it.
setblock 8 1 9 SANDSTONE
wait 30
assert_block 8 1 8 CAKE
assert_block 10 1 8 CAKE
# Front view of the row: eaten sections are missing off each cake's +x
# (left-on-screen) edge; the candle stays a full cube.
camera 8 2.5 5 180 15
wait 20
screenshot bites_front
# Oblique view from +x/+z: each cake's cut (+x) face shows the interior
# tile, shrinking with the bite count.
camera 15 3 12 300 7
wait 20
screenshot bites_inner
echo cake done
